Turnip VK_EXT_external_memory_host on Darwin: a BO over the caller's pages through BlueGPU USERPTR
(bluedrm_user_memory, 16 KiB pages), mapped at the caller's pointer and never unmapped. The
metal2vulkan runtime imports IOSurfaces and no-copy buffers this way. After UniXNU
patches/mesa/turnip-darwin-kmd.patch (MIT), which does the same over its own kernel client.

